flowchart TB
    accTitle: The firmware, physics and calibration loop inside hp-sim5
    accDescr: The autocal program requests sweeps from a measurement collector. Real host-built RepRapFirmware and its bridge turn G-code into motor input for Rust physics, then return observed encoder angles to the collector. Accepted calibration updates the firmware model. The separate USD scene defines the physical machine used in the experiment.

    auto["Autocal program<br/>fit, validate, plan next sweep"]
    collector["Measurement collector<br/>force tuning, settling, sampling"]
    firmware["Real firmware and its bridge<br/>RRF planning, kinematics and transport"]
    physics["Simulated robot<br/>Rust: motors, cables, bodies, encoders"]
    model["Firmware's model<br/>configuration and current calibration"]
    machine["Physical machine definition<br/>.usda scene, loaded and baked"]

    auto <-->|sweep request / measured data| collector
    collector <-->|G-code / sensor replies| firmware
    firmware <-->|motor input / encoder angles| physics
    model -->|parameters| firmware
    machine -->|geometry and dynamics| physics
    auto -. apply accepted calibration .-> model
